 ## Non-CSA qualification v2
 
 The [instrumented aggregate report](results/non-csa-qualification-v2/RESULTS_AND_STATUS.md) records outcome denominators, constructor/resource costs and bounded negative results. Its [evidence scope](results/non-csa-qualification-v2/EVIDENCE_SCOPE.md) identifies the separately retained raw packet and subsequent native check status. Scoped retained TP completed the26-query panel plus78 warm calls; fixed-cap ranked T-REX certified0/26. Global TP construction remained incomplete at180 seconds. These are artifact measurements, with no timing inheritance to this clean public source. Confidence intervals remain unmet.
+
+## Diagnostic profiles
+
+`familybench` optionally accepts `-cpu-profile /new/file.pprof` and
+`-heap-profile /new/heap.pprof`. Paths are exclusively created, never overwritten.
+CPU profiling covers the whole run after output-directory creation, including
+source verification, loading, preparation, queries and artifact encoding. The
+heap/allocations profile is written at ordinary return without an extra GC or
+sampling-rate change. The output directory receives `diagnostic-profiles.json`
+with scope, completion/error status and an explicit timing warning. Existing
+ordinary error/deadline paths flush profiles; abrupt exit/SIGKILL cannot do so
+and may leave an empty metadata file or incomplete profile.
+
+These files are diagnostics only. Run final latency comparisons with both flags
+omitted. Disabled profiling creates no files or metadata and changes no output
+schema or router settings. Build through `scripts/build.sh` as usual; analyze
+with `go tool pprof -top BINARY CPU_PROFILE` or
+`go tool pprof -sample_index=alloc_space BINARY HEAP_PROFILE`.
